        "comments": "The assembly mMyoDau2.hap1.2 is based on 40x PacBio data and Arima2 Hi-C data generated by the Darwin Tree of Life Project\n(https://www.darwintreeoflife.org/). The assembly process included the following sequence of steps: initial PacBio assembly generation with Hifiasm in Hi-C integrated assembly mode, and Hi-C based scaffolding with YaHS. The mitochondrial genome was assembled using MitoHiFi. Finally, each haplotype assembly was analysed and manually improved using TreeVal. Chromosome-scale scaffolds are named by synteny based on Myotis daubentonii (Daubenton's bat) GCA_963259705.1. The X and Y chromosomes were identified based on its single-copy status within a diploid assembly and synteny analysis with Myotis mystacinus (GCA_964094495.2).The exact order and orientation of the contigs on chromosome X (79,320 - 103,100 Kbp) are unknown.The exact order and orientation of the contigs on chromosome Y are unknown.The exact order and orientation of the contigs on chromosome 1 (143,000 - 146,0u00 Kbp) are unknown.The exact order and orientation of the contigs on chromosome 2 (117,624 - 120,600 Kbp) are unknown.",
